{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ugcjk75ijUm3gs9cNNj2Ky","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the Diskless Core design discussion in the context files, **the final agreement was to build a new metadata component independent of RLMM**, rather than reuse the existing RLMM for diskless metadata.\\\\n\\\\nThis is clearly stated in Jun Rao's message from May 12, 2026:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"JR11. I was thinking we leave the existing RLMM as is and continue to use it for classic topics. We design a new, more efficient metadata management component independent of RLMM. This new component will be the only metadata component that diskless topics depend on.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis position was supported by others in the discussion. Satish Duggana responded with:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"+1 to Jun on leaving the existing RLMM for classic topics with tiered storage and having an efficient metadata management system required for diskless topics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe reasoning behind this decision was that RLMM was not designed for the aggressive metadata generation and management requirements of diskless topics, which would involve 20X or more increase in metadata compared to traditional usage.\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n- `events/2026/05/14/mail-eccf8894903dbc34be1145c8-3e3a9a34.md` (Greg Harris's reply, May 14, 2026)\\\\n- `events/2026/05/15/mail-a192cc3ce6018a685014966e-52210511.md` (Jun Rao's response, May 15, 2026)\\\\n- `events/2026/05/15/mail-e4a05c90c512657787366663-d91a6d58.md` (Viktor Somogyi-Vass's response, May 15, 2026)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"events/2026/05/15/mail-e4a05c90c512657787366663-d91a6d58.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/05/15/mail-a192cc3ce6018a685014966e-52210511.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/05/14/mail-eccf8894903dbc34be1145c8-3e3a9a34.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":20.27,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":44052,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":84541,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1800012,\\\"input_tokens\\\":34,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1296}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"947a9983-91f1-476c-8fcc-8cc0696f681b","uuid":"5b8e4d0b-73e9-462f-9dfa-51a24a61597e","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:49:17.044Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the Diskless Core design discussion in the context files, **the final agreement was to build a new metadata component independent of RLMM**, rather than reuse the existing RLMM for diskless metadata.\\\\n\\\\nThis is clearly stated in Jun Rao's message from May 12, 2026:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"JR11. I was thinking we leave the existing RLMM as is and continue to use it for classic topics. We design a new, more efficient metadata management component independent of RLMM. This new component will be the only metadata component that diskless topics depend on.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis position was supported by others in the discussion. Satish Duggana responded with:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"+1 to Jun on leaving the existing RLMM for classic topics with tiered storage and having an efficient metadata management system required for diskless topics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe reasoning behind this decision was that RLMM was not designed for the aggressive metadata generation and management requirements of diskless topics, which would involve 20X or more increase in metadata compared to traditional usage.\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n- `events/2026/05/14/mail-eccf8894903dbc34be1145c8-3e3a9a34.md` (Greg Harris's reply, May 14, 2026)\\\\n- `events/2026/05/15/mail-a192cc3ce6018a685014966e-52210511.md` (Jun Rao's response, May 15, 2026)\\\\n- `events/2026/05/15/mail-e4a05c90c512657787366663-d91a6d58.md` (Viktor Somogyi-Vass's response, May 15, 2026)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"events/2026/05/15/mail-e4a05c90c512657787366663-d91a6d58.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/05/15/mail-a192cc3ce6018a685014966e-52210511.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/05/14/mail-eccf8894903dbc34be1145c8-3e3a9a34.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":20.27,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":44052,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":84541,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.1800012,\\\"input_tokens\\\":34,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1296}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on the Diskless Core design discussion in the context files, **the final agreement was to build a new metadata component independent of RLMM**, rather than reuse the existing RLMM for diskless metadata.\\n\\nThis is clearly stated in Jun Rao's message from May 12, 2026:\\n\\n> \\\"JR11. I was thinking we leave the existing RLMM as is and continue to use it for classic topics. We design a new, more efficient metadata management component independent of RLMM. This new component will be the only metadata component that diskless topics depend on.\\\"\\n\\nThis position was supported by others in the discussion. Satish Duggana responded with:\\n\\n> \\\"+1 to Jun on leaving the existing RLMM for classic topics with tiered storage and having an efficient metadata management system required for diskless topics.\\\"\\n\\nThe reasoning behind this decision was that RLMM was not designed for the aggressive metadata generation and management requirements of diskless topics, which would involve 20X or more increase in metadata compared to traditional usage.\\n\\n**Sources:**\\n- `events/2026/05/14/mail-eccf8894903dbc34be1145c8-3e3a9a34.md` (Greg Harris's reply, May 14, 2026)\\n- `events/2026/05/15/mail-a192cc3ce6018a685014966e-52210511.md` (Jun Rao's response, May 15, 2026)\\n- `events/2026/05/15/mail-e4a05c90c512657787366663-d91a6d58.md` (Viktor Somogyi-Vass's response, May 15, 2026)\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"events/2026/05/15/mail-e4a05c90c512657787366663-d91a6d58.md\",\"events/2026/05/15/mail-a192cc3ce6018a685014966e-52210511.md\",\"events/2026/05/14/mail-eccf8894903dbc34be1145c8-3e3a9a34.md\"],\"seconds\":20.27,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":2,\"usage\":{\